<details class="performance-notes" id="periodic-calculation-notes">
  <summary>Provisional calculation rules and assumptions</summary>
  <p>These defaults were authorized for implementation while awaiting Hadi's review. They are not Hadi-confirmed definitions, except Debt at RED as unfinished expected work.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Includes every day from RSD through RED. Beginning debt uses status at the end of the day before RSD, open with current due date before RSD. New is not an excluded status for this Periodic report.</li>
    <li>Current Ticket Owner governs all attribution, including old periods. Current blank owners stay unassigned. Current due date, tracker, priority and visible Complexity Weight apply; later edits can change historical results.</li>
    <li>Recorded assignment means the latest real Ticket Owner change into the current owner on/before RED, including initial assignments. No assignment record means unknown, not ticket creation. Native assignee changes are not used.</li>
    <li>Category precedence is beginning debt, then hotfix, then planned task. Tickets already closed before RSD are outside expectation. Planned tasks have a current due date within the period, including assignments made before RSD and tickets created during the period.</li>
    <li>Hotfix means current priority Immediate/Hot Fix, with recorded assignment to the current owner during the period. Urgent/Current Week alone is not a hotfix. A hotfix qualifies even with no due date or a due date outside the period. Its expected date is an in-period due date, otherwise its assignment date.</li>
    <li>Archived, Ongoing and On-Hold at RED are excluded from the entire expectation and actual package, with a linked exclusion list. Beginning debt also requires an eligible opening status. This provisional removal rule awaits confirmation.</li>
    <li>Actual delivery requires Done / Closed at RED and a recorded transition into that status within RSD–RED. Each ticket counts once using its latest completion. Reopening before RED removes delivery; reopening after RED does not. Missing completion evidence is disclosed; expected work without qualifying completion remains unresolved in debt.</li>
    <li>Other Done is qualifying delivery outside the expectation package. It increases Total Actual Done, never Completed from Expectation or its deviation. Logged time, comments and progress alone are not completion.</li>
    <li>Debt at RED = Expected Total minus Completed from Expectation. Still Open Now is its currently non-closed subset; this current follow-up includes On-Hold/Ongoing if they are open now. Existing PMO debt rules remain unchanged.</li>
    <li>Debt targets are zero, while actual beginning-debt workload contributes to expectation. Expected-work deviation is Completed from Expectation minus Expected Total. Debt and Other Done use Plan minus Actual. Total Actual Done has a separate output comparison against Expected Total. Positive is good, negative bad, zero neutral; zero-plan percentages are N/A.</li>
    <li>Counts and usable weights use distinct tickets. Team totals are sums; percentages use those totals, not averages of owner percentages. Missing/hidden/nonpositive/nonfinite weights add no points and are reported separately.</li>
    <li>Trend packages use RED eligibility throughout. Expected follows current due dates and the hotfix fallback above, with beginning debt at the opening point. Actual follows recorded completions for tickets still Done / Closed at RED. Monday–Sunday weeks have partial first/last weeks; periods over 120 days use month ends. Endpoints reconcile to the cards.</li>
    <li>Initial navigation does not scan tickets or history. Apply uses visible projects/issues and visible Ticket Owner fields. Details recalculate the same sets under current permissions; edits between requests may change results. No snapshot database, new custom fields or stored counters are created.</li>
  </ul>
</details>
